README

The Raspberry Pi foundation maintains a fork of OpenOCD: https://github.com/raspberrypi/openocd that has the parts for working with the RP2040.

Following their instructions in Chapter 5 in [https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/pico/getting-started-with-pico.pdf](https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/pico/getting-started-with-pico.pdf), we can download OpenOCD, build it, and execute it.  

In fact, the executable can be used in other RPis, something we take advantage of: our Pioreactor image has this executable.

The current executable `openocd` was compiled on the Raspberry Pi:

Operating system:       Linux-6.12.47+rpt-rpi-v8-aarch64-with-glibc2.41
Raspberry Pi:           Raspberry Pi 5


with compile options:

```
./configure --enable-bcm2835gpio --disable-werror --enable-linuxgpiod
```